Minimized ABI reproducers.

Every file here is a signature descriptor (abigen's text form) that once made
cgfried and the reference compiler disagree, shrunk by the lane's minimizer
until dropping any argument or unwrapping any composite made the failure go
away. scripts/abi_differential_lane.sh replays all of them before it generates
anything, on every target it runs.

They are kept because a generated seed only covers a shape until the generator
changes; these are the shapes that actually broke. New ones are written here
automatically when the lane finds a disagreement -- check in the minimal
descriptor, not the whole generated program, since abigen regenerates the
sources from it deterministically.

  x86_64-sysv-split-eightbyte
      SysV 3.2.3 step 5. Three integer scalars fill rdi/rsi/rdx and a 16-byte
      composite takes rcx/r8, so a following 15-byte composite has one
      register left for its two eightbytes. We split it -- first half in r9,
      second on the stack -- where the psABI says an argument that cannot be
      placed entirely in registers goes entirely in memory.

  aapcs64-hfa-exhaust-d4, -f4, -f3
      AAPCS64 C.4. Two HFAs with a scalar double between them need nine SIMD
      registers and there are eight. The second HFA must go on the stack
      whole, and NSRN is then pinned at 8 so later FP arguments stack too. We
      placed the leaves one at a time and split the aggregate across v-regs
      and memory.

Both bugs failed in BOTH directions, which is the tell for a self-consistent
convention error: our caller and our callee agreed with each other and neither
agreed with gcc. A same-compiler test cannot see that.
